GGL Applications using the GGL Common Library
---------------------------------------------

gpskin:

Author: Marc Cocard <cocard@geod.ethz.ch>
A small tool to calculate GPS day, day of year, modified julian date,
etc. from any of those values as input.
This program is interactive and menu driven.

trafo:

Author: Etienne Favey <favey@geod.ethz.ch>
Perform coordinate transformations between Swiss Military Projection,
WGS, ITRF, and the like. The supported list of geodetic datums is
incomplete and probably always will be.
Type `trafo -h' for a short introduction.

natra:

Author: Etienne Favey <favey@geod.ethz.ch>
Perform coordinate transformations between two freely defined reference
frames, doing only translation and rotation (scaling suppressed).
The systems have to be right handed. You have to supply controlpoints
in both systems. The transformation parameters will be derived by LSM.
Type `natra -h' for a short introduction.


